  actor: jgstern_agent  # 6250
  clock: 6  # 6250
  nonce: '6250'  # 6250
  message: "IMPLEMENTED AND GREEN, AWAITING YOUR MERGE: PR #977, pushed with --gov so CI ran\nbut the merge is yours. AGENTS.md's no-self-merge rule on scripts/auto-pr and\n.githooks/** is unambiguous, and I would rather you take that action than have me\nread the standing autonomy ruling broadly.\n\nTHE PREMISE HELD AND THE RISK WAS REAL, which is why the design has a piece the\nfiled version did not. Verification results are in the previous message. The\nshort version: a hook peeking with a fresh open() sees the lock even as a\nDESCENDANT holding the inherited fd (the concern I filed this item with is\nresolved), but every git and curl auto-pr forks inherits the lock fd and bash has\nno close-on-exec escape, so a SIGKILLed run keeps the lock until its orphans\nexit. A naive conversion would have traded a loud 15-minute window for a silent\npermanent one. The lock therefore records pid/started -- SyncGate's own body\nshape -- and the detector asks whether the recorded owner is still alive.\n\nACCEPTANCE, against the REAL hooks and the REAL acquire function extracted from\nauto-pr rather than re-implemented:\n\n  no file                    -> both hooks recover\n  lock held by a live holder -> both hooks skip\n  holder killed, file left   -> both hooks recover   <- the ten-hour bug, gone\n  leftover flag file         -> both hooks recover\n  orphan child holds lock    -> both hooks skip\n  orphan child exits         -> both hooks recover\n\nHook suite 45 passed / 0 failed, including two NEW difference arms asserting that\nan UNHELD leftover file suppresses nothing. Those are the arms that fail against\nthe defect; without them the suite would pass just as happily on the old code.\nPython: 4381 passed, tracker package 100% in isolation, ratchet 669 delta +0.\n\nWHAT THIS DELETES. _UNOWNED_GRACE_SECONDS, and with it the whole business of\nmeasuring auto-pr's phases to pick a number -- including the 900s I measured and\nshipped a few hours earlier in PR #976. A lock answers \"is anybody there\" as a\nfact. I would rather delete a constant than keep one that has to be re-measured\nevery time auto-pr's phases move.\n\nTHE PRIORITY QUESTION I RAISED EARLIER IS NOW MOOT for scheduling purposes, but\nthe answer still belongs to you if you want it on the record."  # 6250
